==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|la|ētās||Medieval}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₂ey-|id=life}}
[[syncope|Syncope]] of earlier {{m|la|aevitās}}, from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*aiwotāts}}, from {{m|itc-pro|*aiwom}} ((whence also {{m|la|aevum}}) from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂eyu-||lifetime}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂ey-||vital energy, life}}) + {{m|itc-pro|*-tāts}} (whence also {{m|la|-tās}}). {{surf|la|aevum|-tās}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|aetās}}
* {{rhymes|la|aːs|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|aetās<3>|acc_pl=aetātīs/aetātēs}}

# {{lb|la|principally}}  the [[period]] of a life: [[lifetime]], [[lifespan]]
# [[time]] of [[life]], [[period]] of [[life]], [[age]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|5|353-354|quote=et monet '''aetātis''' speciē, dum flōreat, ūtī;<br/>contemnī spīnam, cum cecidēre rosae|trans=''And she urges [us] to indulge in the sight of [young] '''age''', while [it is] still in bloom: The thorn is despised when the roses have fallen.''<br/>(“She” is {{w|Flora (mythology)}}.)}}
# an [[undefined]], particularly long [[period]] of time: an [[age]], an [[era]], a [[term]], a [[duration]]
# {{lb|la|metonymic}} a [[generation]]

